ith control / REFUSE counts with controls / PINS (start, mid, verdict, branch name beside each sha) / instrument and load (dotnet, node, npm versions; load and slot per heavy run; every wait; every `gh` and Jira GET named) / the invariants and the prediction (written before any run, with their evidence paths) / C1-C10 each with the FAIL (clock time), evidence path and result / **the round-1 closure table (B533-1 to B533-7: closed / open / new, with the proof)** / the Done-when clause table / the removed-lines tables (33 against base; 6 round-1 lines) / the new-names table (31 plus the changed row: red or green at `25cb365` and at base, killing mutant) / the mutant table and the rows table / the attack-row table (id, request shape, expected, answer, stored state, host, MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY) / the C6 table (generator power, differential counts, exhaustive space, capability grading per shape) / findings `B545-n` (severity, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, closure state, fix-shape in prose, the regression that would be red; "none" is valid) / findings of FACT for Tuesday listed apart (anything the diff leaves standing and base had equally: the free fields that move money, rental credits and the sibling lane that owns them, the quadratic shapes and the input cap owned elsewhere, the echo of a request string into a 403 detail if base has it, the `listPrice` naming question, the squash message and the trailer-less commit, D-1's withdrawal and the save-time refusal still unbuilt) / **ROUND-CAP STATEMENT: closed instances that ship, open or new instances to ticket** / FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections (where the fix STATUS or this brief was wrong, with the measurement) / processes, slots, trees left / **UNMEASURED** (last section before the last line: the CI Linux runner beyond the PR logs, behaviour on a real hosted site and with real data, the `python` and `package` jobs, a signed-in browser, the merged result's build with ma